# Unemployment Analysis in India — Impact of COVID-19

Exploratory data analysis of unemployment trends across Indian states (Jan 2019 – Oct 2020), 
with a focus on how the COVID-19 lockdown affected regional labour markets.

## 📊 What this covers
- Data cleaning & type conversion (dates, numeric fields, whitespace artifacts)
- Region-wise and month-wise unemployment trends
- Time-series comparison across 5 major states (Maharashtra, UP, Tamil Nadu, Delhi, West Bengal)
- Top 10 states by average unemployment rate
- Correlation heatmap: unemployment rate, employment rate, labour participation rate
- Pre-COVID vs. post-COVID comparison (cutoff: 25 March 2020, India's lockdown date)

## 🔑 Key finding
All-India average unemployment rate nearly **doubled** post-lockdown (9.5% → 17.8%), 
alongside a **drop in labour participation rate** (43.9% → 39.3%) — suggesting many people 
exited the workforce entirely rather than simply staying unemployed while job-hunting.

## 🛠 Tech stack
Python · pandas · matplotlib · seaborn · Jupyter Notebook

## 📁 Dataset
["Unemployment in India"](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/gokulrajkmv/unemployment-in-india) 
by Gokul Raj Kumar V (sourced from CMIE — Centre for Monitoring Indian Economy).

## 🚀 Running it
```bash
pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn jupyter
jupyter notebook Unemployment_Analysis_India.ipynb
```

